After loading, we need to verify loading profile (candidate_loading_verified) and stage for loading (candidate_staged_for_loading). There are actions verify_loading_profile_nominal and verify_loading_profile_destination_flag. Which one? Goal does not require destination_leg_loaded or origin_leg_loaded. So we can use nominal (neither origin nor destination leg loaded). Since we haven't loaded origin or destination leg (those are about origin_leg_loaded/destination_leg_loaded predicates on transport leg). We have not set those. So we can use verify_loading_profile_nominal. Preconditions: candidate_staged_for_loading ?candidate, candidate_skill_certificate_linked ?candidate ?skill_certificate, candidate_operator_linked ?candidate ?operator_resource, candidate_loading_container_linked ?candidate ?loading_container, loading_container_leg_linked ?loading_container ?transport_leg, loading_container_loaded ?loading_container? Wait check: verify_loading_profile_nominal precondition includes loading_container_leg_linked ?loading_container ?transport_leg and loading_container_loaded ?loading_container? Let's look: In domain:

(:action verify_loading_profile_nominal
    :parameters (?candidate - schedule_candidate ?skill_certificate - skill_certificate ?operator_resource - operator_resource ?loading_container - loading_container ?transport_leg - transport_leg)
    :precondition
      (and
        (candidate_staged_for_loading ?candidate)
        (candidate_skill_certificate_linked ?candidate ?skill_certificate)
        (candidate_operator_linked ?candidate ?operator_resource)
        (candidate_loading_container_linked ?candidate ?loading_container)
        (loading_container_leg_linked ?loading_container ?transport_leg)
        (not
          (destination_leg_loaded ?transport_leg)
        )
        (not
          (candidate_loading_verified ?candidate)
        )
      )
    :effect (candidate_loading_verified ?candidate)

Thus we need candidate_staged_for_loading first. There's action stage_schedule_candidate:

(:action stage_schedule_candidate
    :parameters (?candidate - schedule_candidate ?loading_container - loading_container ?transport_leg - transport_leg ?route_task_profile - route_task_profile)
    :precondition
      (and
        (candidate_prepared ?candidate)
        (candidate_loading_container_linked ?candidate ?loading_container)
        (loading_container_loaded ?loading_container)
        (loading_container_leg_linked ?loading_container ?transport_leg)
        (candidate_task_profile_linked ?candidate ?route_task_profile)
        (not
          (origin_leg_loaded ?transport_leg)
        )
        (not
          (candidate_staged_for_loading ?candidate)
        )
      )
    :effect (candidate_staged_for_loading ?candidate)

Thus we need loading_container_loaded and loading_container_leg_linked before we can stage. So sequence: load container onto leg (sets loading_container_loaded and loading_container_leg_linked), then stage schedule candidate (requires those), then verify loading profile (requires candidate_staged_for_loading, skill cert link, operator link, loading container linked, loading_container_leg_linked, not destination_leg_loaded, not candidate_loading_verified). After verify, we get candidate_loading_verified.

